# Engine / nodes — realtime safety

These paths participate in or sit adjacent to the audio graph. Match the intent of Claude Code’s PostToolUse hook in [`.claude/settings.local.json`](.claude/settings.local.json).

## Avoid on the realtime / audio callback path

Unless explicitly outside the audio thread (e.g. `prepareToRender`, `releaseResources`, `getState` / `setState`, or clearly commented message-thread-only code):

- Heap allocation: `new`, `delete`, `malloc`, `free`, containers that allocate
- Mutexes, lock guards, `CriticalSection`, `SpinLock`, `unique_lock`
- Blocking I/O or unbounded waiting

Prefer patterns documented in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) (Real-time Safety): pre-allocation in `prepareToRender`, atomics, lock-free handoff, `juce::AbstractFifo`, etc.

## Escape hatch (aligns with existing hook convention)

If a deliberate exception is required in a hot path, add an explicit comment such as `// no-rt-check` and a short justification so reviewers (and future grep) can tell it apart from accidental regressions.
